Keep the application alive once a browser has launched it

On the web, Platform::run returns at once and the page drives the event
loop, so the application was dropped as soon as it finished launching,
and with it every window and the closures the page calls them through.

License: Apache-2.0 (Zed v1.6.3)

--- a/crates/gpui/src/app.rs
+++ b/crates/gpui/src/app.rs
@@ -207,6 +207,12 @@
             let cx = &mut *this.borrow_mut();
             on_finish_launching(cx);
         }));
+        // A browser's run returns at once, leaving the event loop to the page,
+        // so nothing would hold the application once it finished launching:
+        // it lives as long as the page instead, as it lives as long as the
+        // process where run never returns.
+        #[cfg(target_family = "wasm")]
+        std::mem::forget(self);
     }
 
     /// Register a handler to be invoked when the platform instructs the application
